    "question": "A monkey swings from branch to branch at an average distance of 1.2 meters per second. How far will a monkey swing in meters if it consistently swings from branches for 30 minutes?",
    "gold": "2160",
    "answer": "If a monkey swings 1.2 meters a second then a monkey can swing 1.2 meters/second * 60 seconds/minute = <<1.2*60=72>>72 meters in a minute.\nIf a monkey swings 72 meters in a minute then a monkey can swing 72 meters/min * 30 minutes = <<72*30=2160>>2,160 meters in 30 minutes\n#### 2160"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how far a monkey will swing in 30 minutes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the time from minutes to seconds:**\n   Since there are 60 seconds in a minute, we can convert 30 minutes to seconds by multiplying 30 by 60.\n   \\[\n   30 \\text{ minutes} \\times 60 \\text{ seconds/minute} = 1800 \\text{ seconds}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total distance swung:**\n   The monkey swings at an average distance of 1.2 meters per second. To find the total distance swung in 1800 seconds, we multiply the average distance per second by the total time in seconds.\n   \\[\n   1.2 \\text{ meters/second} \\times 1800 \\text{ seconds} = 2160 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total distance the monkey will swing in 30 minutes is \\(\\boxed{2160}\\) meters.",
